The threat model and the configuration reference now say that `.vault/config` is plaintext, committed and unsigned, and that it names who may sign records and who the next `seal` encrypts to, so a change to it is a change to the trust root and should be reviewed like code. They also spell out that a key named only in a `wrap` rule can sign a record for any path, such as `~/.bashrc`, and every machine that unseals writes it.
